                        "entry_id": "30446789-6801-341a-93f0-bbb02008e957",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who wants, or who wants something"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2341f5d6-fcae-44dc-9a84-c138806a8040",
                                "sense_id": "c5884919-9f9b-337c-8a4f-f7ac680506f9",
                                "text": "Witless hizzie, e'en 's you like, The ne'er a doit I 'm carin'; But men maun be the first to speak, An' wanters maun be speerin'."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4008df8d-0755-4255-9f72-ebe555ddcb45",
                                "sense_id": "c5884919-9f9b-337c-8a4f-f7ac680506f9",
                                "text": "But if Donald McFarlane wants money, he's got kin that can accommodate him, James; wanters arena always that fortunate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4bb14c4-9dc3-4cb2-967d-cead6cfa6a9e",
                                "sense_id": "c5884919-9f9b-337c-8a4f-f7ac680506f9",
                                "text": "You see, the trouble with Americans is that they are the greatest wanters of cake after they've eaten it the world has ever seen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f753453c-4453-4010-a3b6-7111cc898acb",
                                "sense_id": "c5884919-9f9b-337c-8a4f-f7ac680506f9",
                                "text": "She’s continually the wanter in a relationship but dreams of being the one wanted, which is to say she’s continually powerless, dreaming of power."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
